WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:05.674
Cooking class was over.

2
00:00:05.675 --> 00:00:09.224
As Jason hung up his apron, his phone beeped.

3
00:00:09.225 --> 00:00:12.063
So did his friends' phones.

4
00:00:12.064 --> 00:00:16.378
"It's a video from Ethan!" Jason said.

5
00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:20.003
As he played it, everyone watched.

6
00:00:20.004 --> 00:00:22.875
Even Chef was interested.

7
00:00:22.876 --> 00:00:26.404
"It's Ethan surfing," Bobby said.

8
00:00:26.405 --> 00:00:29.778
"He's a great athlete."

9
00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:34.213
"He's so tanned!" Nina said.

10
00:00:34.214 --> 00:00:39.714
Izzie sighed. "Isn't he cool?"

11
00:00:39.715 --> 00:00:42.048
Jason rolled his eyes.

12
00:00:42.049 --> 00:00:45.451
"I bet he wiped out a lot before this video."

13
00:00:45.452 --> 00:00:49.589
"You're just jealous," Izzie said.

14
00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.126
Ethan sent another video.

15
00:00:52.127 --> 00:00:56.461
In this one, he was ordering fish tacos from a food truck.

16
00:00:56.462 --> 00:01:01.514
His text said, Hope everyone is having a great summer!

17
00:01:01.515 --> 00:01:04.298
"Hmm," Chef said.

18
00:01:04.299 --> 00:01:08.060
"Why don't we make fish tacos in our next class?"

19
00:01:08.061 --> 00:01:14.775
Everyone cheered, except for Jason.

20
00:01:14.776 --> 00:01:18.913
*** The next day Jason was excited to show off his new

21
00:01:18.914 --> 00:01:24.172
look. He felt cool in his sunglasses, tank top, and

22
00:01:24.173 --> 00:01:31.934
flip-flops. "Maybe nobody will notice my sunburn," he

23
00:01:31.935 --> 00:01:35.141
thought. His friends stared at him as he walked

24
00:01:35.142 --> 00:01:38.205
in. But nobody said

25
00:01:38.206 --> 00:01:40.622
anything. Chef pointed to the

26
00:01:40.623 --> 00:01:43.346
screen. "There's our fish taco

27
00:01:43.347 --> 00:01:46.709
recipe. Let's start chopping

28
00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:50.495
vegetables." The kids chopped cabbage and red

29
00:01:50.496 --> 00:01:54.963
onion. "Jason, you're sunburned!" Nina

30
00:01:54.964 --> 00:01:59.837
said. Izzie frowned. "Sunburn harms your

31
00:01:59.838 --> 00:02:02.576
skin. You should wear

32
00:02:02.577 --> 00:02:04.621
sunscreen." Jason

33
00:02:04.622 --> 00:02:08.215
shrugged. "I was just soaking up some

34
00:02:08.216 --> 00:02:11.877
rays." "Jason, please juice the lime," Chef

35
00:02:11.878 --> 00:02:15.314
said. "And take off those

36
00:02:15.315 --> 00:02:17.621
sunglasses." "I can see

37
00:02:17.622 --> 00:02:22.924
fine." "Take them off! You don't need them

38
00:02:22.925 --> 00:02:26.397
inside." Jason sighed and put on his regular

39
00:02:26.398 --> 00:02:30.285
glasses. He had white circles around his

40
00:02:30.286 --> 00:02:35.879
eyes. Bobby chuckled. "Nice

41
00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.427
look!" Jason ignored him and juiced the lime.

42
00:02:40.428 --> 00:02:43.878
Then he poured the juice over the vegetables.

43
00:02:43.879 --> 00:02:47.271
Izzie added sour cream.

44
00:02:47.272 --> 00:02:52.447
Nina sprinkled in salt and stirred the ingredients together.

45
00:02:52.448 --> 00:02:57.443
Bobby put the bowl in the refrigerator to chill.

46
00:02:57.444 --> 00:03:02.568
"Now we mix the spices for the fish," Chef said.

47
00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:06.165
Bobby measured garlic powder.

48
00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:09.753
Nina poured in cumin.

49
00:03:09.754 --> 00:03:13.831
Jason measured the cayenne pepper.

50
00:03:13.832 --> 00:03:19.792
Izzie added salt and black pepper, and stirred everything.

51
00:03:19.793 --> 00:03:26.857
Chef seasoned the fish.

52
00:03:26.858 --> 00:03:31.832
Izzie added oil to a pan and turned the heat to medium-high.

53
00:03:31.833 --> 00:03:35.556
"Nina, please chop cilantro," Chef said.

54
00:03:35.557 --> 00:03:42.148
"Bobby, cut lime wedges."

55
00:03:42.149 --> 00:03:44.778
Chef cooked the fish.

56
00:03:44.779 --> 00:03:47.470
Then he put the fillets on a plate.

57
00:03:47.471 --> 00:03:51.730
"Izzie and Jason, break these into pieces."

58
00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:54.104
Jason gave him a thumbs-up.

59
00:03:54.105 --> 00:03:56.772
"Sure thing, dude."

60
00:03:56.773 --> 00:04:01.418
The other kids burst out laughing.

61
00:04:01.419 --> 00:04:04.747
"What's so funny?" Jason snapped.

62
00:04:04.748 --> 00:04:08.574
"You're not being yourself," Bobby said.

63
00:04:08.575 --> 00:04:20.449
Jason frowned. "I'm tired of being myself. I'm trying something new."

64
00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:26.373
Chef heated another pan and warmed the tortillas on both sides.

65
00:04:26.374 --> 00:04:29.629
"Now we can build our tacos."

66
00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:33.608
The kids put the vegetables and fish into the warm tortillas.

67
00:04:33.616 --> 00:04:40.623
They each added cilantro and a squeeze of lime.

68
00:04:40.624 --> 00:04:42.930
Nina looked at Jason.

69
00:04:42.931 --> 00:04:45.965
"Trying new things is fine.

70
00:04:45.966 --> 00:04:50.779
I used to play the flute, but now I'm learning piano."

71
00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:55.734
"Just whatever you do, be yourself," Izzie said.

72
00:04:55.735 --> 00:04:58.247
Jason took a bite of taco.

73
00:04:58.248 --> 00:05:00.937
It was crunchy and delicious.

74
00:05:00.938 --> 00:05:03.948
"I guess you're right," he said.

75
00:05:03.949 --> 00:05:06.963
"I feel silly trying Ethan things.

76
00:05:06.964 --> 00:05:10.728
Next time I'll try new Jason things."

77
00:05:10.729 --> 00:05:17.503
Bobby grinned. "Sounds like a wise idea, dude!"

